# Code owners for go-jupyter. Owners are auto-requested for review on PRs that
# touch their paths, and an owner's approval is required to merge.
#
# Order matters: the LAST matching pattern wins for a given file, and its owners
# are alternatives (any one of them can clear it). Rules do NOT accumulate per
# file — but a PR must satisfy the winning rule of every file it touches, so a
# PR spanning a skill and a terraform file still needs @kltm.

# Default owner for the repo (infra/config): hub config, terraform, systemd,
# scripts, CI, and this file.
*                                                   @kltm

# Curator-authored content — skills, template docs, exercises, news, and the
# prose trees: the GO-CAM skills editor-in-chief or the repo owner reviews.
/user-templates/                                    @pgaudet @kltm

# ...except environment config inside the templates: that is infrastructure,
# not curator content. `**` rather than `*` on purpose — `**` matches zero or
# more directory levels, so a nested copy cannot slip under the content rule.
/user-templates/**/.mcp.json                        @kltm
/user-templates/**/.bashrc                          @kltm
/user-templates/**/.profile                         @kltm
/user-templates/**/.claude/settings.json            @kltm
